Overview
Designed and implemented an automated EC2 Instance Scheduler solution to reduce AWS infrastructure costs by automatically starting and stopping non-production instances based on predefined schedules.
Features
Automated EC2 Start/Stop Operations
Scheduled execution using Amazon EventBridge
Serverless architecture using AWS Lambda
Tag-based instance management
CloudWatch logging for monitoring and troubleshooting
Cost optimization for development and testing environments
Scalable across multiple AWS accounts and regions

Architecture
Amazon EventBridge
        │
        ▼
AWS Lambda Function
        │
        ▼
EC2 API Calls
(Start / Stop Instances)
        │
        ▼
CloudWatch Logs

EventBridge Configuration
Start Schedule
Rule Name: ec2-start-scheduler

Cron Expression:
cron(30 3 ? * MON-FRI *)

Execution Time:
09:00 AM IST (Monday–Friday)
Stop Schedule
Rule Name: ec2-stop-scheduler

Cron Expression:
cron(30 13 ? * MON-FRI *)

Execution Time:
07:00 PM IST (Monday–Friday)
(Adjust according to your actual schedule.)
Lambda Function Responsibilities
Identify instances based on tags.
Verify current instance state.
Start stopped instances during business hours.
Stop running instances after business hours.
Log all actions to CloudWatch Logs.
Handle exceptions and API failures gracefully.
